{{- if eq .Name "braze_catalog" }}

~> Changing the catalog's name, description, or fields replaces it and deletes
all contained items. Add the catalog resource to each managed item's
`lifecycle.replace_triggered_by` to recreate those items when the catalog is
replaced. Back up items managed outside Terraform before applying a replacement.
{{- else if eq .Name "braze_catalog_item" }}

Updates replace all item values. Include every field you want to keep in
`values_json`; omitting a field removes it. Use `jsonencode` for Terraform values
and leave the Braze `id` field out of the JSON object, because `item_id` identifies
the item.

When Terraform also manages the catalog, use `replace_triggered_by` as shown
below. Replacing a catalog deletes its items, even if its name stays the same.
{{- else if or (eq .Name "braze_content_block") (eq .Name "braze_email_template") }}

~> Destroy removes Terraform state only; the remote object remains in Braze.
Replacement leaves the previous object behind, even if a forced `-replace` plan
does not display a warning. Import an existing object to resume management.
{{- end }}

